---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

import Collection from "../components/Collection.astro";
import RootLayout from "../layouts/RootLayout.astro";
import PageWithSideBarNav from "@/layouts/PageWithSideBarNav.astro";
const pageTitle = "Federal Agency Links";

// TODO: get posts for each question on this page
const posts = await getCollection("programPost", ({ data }) => {
  return data.programArea === "Acquisition";
});
---

<RootLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <PageWithSideBarNav>
    <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
    <div class="usa-prose">
      <p>
        The Federal Agency Links page provides links to the Environmental Home
        Pages of various Federal agencies. <a
          href="/programs/compliance/stateprograms/"
          target="new">Click here</a
        > to access environmental home pages for all 50 U.S. states.
        <!-- TODO: Add a link here -->
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="prg#Attributes.StylesPrefix#Container">
      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=470&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          Air Force Civil Engineer Center</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        The Air Force Civil Engineer Center provides Air Force leaders with the
        comprehensive expertise and professional services necessary to protect,
        preserve, restore, develop and sustain the nation's environmental and
        installation resources.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=7749&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          Air Force Installations, Environment and Energy</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        Office of the Assistant Secretary of the Air Force's home page for
        installations, environment, and energy.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=17702&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          Army Regional Environmental and Energy Offices</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        The Army Regional Environmental and Energy Offices protect and advance
        Army (and DoD) military readiness by engaging State governments,
        regional Federal agencies and non-governmental organizations to promote
        sustainable installation operations. The Army has four Regional
        Environmental and Energy Offices (REEOs); the Northern Office at
        Aberdeen Proving Ground, Southern Office in Atlanta, Central Office in
        Kansas City, and Western Office in Denver. Army is the lead DoD REC for
        USEPA Region 5 (Northern Office), Region 4 (Southern Office), Region 7
        (Central Office), and Region 8 (Western Office).
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=14766&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          CIAQ - Federal Interagency Committee on Indoor Air Quality</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        Charged by Congress (1983) with coordinating public/private research on
        indoor air quality; 24 member agencies. Public webinars/meetings with
        presentations and member agency updates in February, June and October.
        Email: CIAQ@epa.gov , Listserve: ciaq-subscribe@lists.epa.gov.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=548&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          Defense Environmental Network &amp; Information eXchange (DENIX)</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        DENIX is the central platform and information clearinghouse for
        environment, safety and occupational health (ESOH) news, information,
        policy, and guidance. Serving the worldwide greater Department of
        Defense (DoD) community, DENIX offers ESOH professionals a vast document
        library, a gateway to web-based environmental compliance tools, an
        interactive workgroup environment, a variety of groupware tools and an
        active membership community numbering thousands.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=19690&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          Department of Defense (DoD) Natural Resources Program</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        The DoD Natural Resources Program (NR Program) supports the military's
        testing and training mission by protecting its biological resources. The
        NR Program provides policy, guidance, and oversight for management of
        natural resources on approximately 27 million acres of military land,
        air, and water resources owned or operated by DoD. The NR Program's goal
        is to support the military's combat readiness mission by ensuring
        continued access to realistic habitat conditions, while simultaneously
        working to ensure the long-term sustainability of our nation's priceless
        natural heritage.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=9909&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          Department of Justice Environmental Programs</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        The intent of these pages is to facilitate and communicate DOJ's
        commitment to serving as an example in the area of environmental
        stewardship and compliance with environmental legislation and Executive
        Orders.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=33532&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          Federal Green Challenge Website</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        The Federal Green Challenge (FGC) is a national effort under EPA's
        Sustainable Materials Management Program, challenging EPA and other
        federal agencies throughout the country to lead by example in reducing
        the federal government's environmental impact. It furthers the goals of
        the President's Executive Order Regarding Efficient Federal Operations.
        This website provides federal installations guidance on reducing,
        reusing, and recycling resources.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=895&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          GSA's Public Building Service Environmental Program</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        The Public Buildings Service’s environmental goal is to eliminate all
        damage to the environment resulting from its operations. The PBS
        Environment Program works in coordination with the Sustainable Design
        and Energy programs to ensure that PBS continuously makes progress
        towards that goal.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=10308&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          Internal Revenue Service (IRS) Environmental Program</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        The IRS environmental home page. Provides links to information on
        program elements, roles and responsibilities, training, inspections,
        audits, and assessments.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=893&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          NASA's Environmental Management Division</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        NASA's Environmental Management Division serves as Agency lead in
        assuring that NASA meets its Federal stewardship responsibilities and
        achieves sustainability while carrying out its primary mission of
        understanding and protecting our home planet, exploring the Universe and
        searching for life, and inspiring the next generation of explorers.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=59&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          Office of Federal Sustainability (OFS)</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        Promoting sustainable environmental stewardship throughout the federal
        government.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=918&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          U.S. Army Corps of Engineers' Environmental Community of Practice</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        The Environmental Community of Practice (eCoP) provides the public with
        a central point to access information on all the U.S. Army Corps of
        Engineers environmental programs. The Corps supports or manages numerous
        environmental initiatives including Ecosystem Restoration, Formerly Used
        Defense Sites, Environmental Stewardship, support to EPA Superfund and
        Brownfields programs, Abandoned Mine Lands, Formerly Utilized Sites
        Remedial Action Program, Base Realignment and Closure 2005, and
        Regulatory. The Corps' environmental programs support the warfighter and
        military installations worldwide as well as the Corps' public recreation
        facilities throughout the country.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=471&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          U.S. Army Environmental Command</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        USAEC is the Army's point organization for implementing environmental
        programs that enhance Army training and operations while protecting the
        environment. As a field-operating agency of the ACSIM, USAEC's mission
        implements the environmental program for the Army by providing a broad
        range of innovative and cost-effective products and services in support
        of Army training, operations, and sound stewardship.
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemHeader">
        <a href="/Bookmarks/index.cfm?id=60&pge_prg_id=8693&pge_id=1852">
          US EPA - Office of Enforcement and Compliance Assurance (OECA)</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="prgItemDescription" style="padding-left:20px;">
        Responsible for ensuring the compliance of the regulated community with
        federal environmental statutes.
      </div>
    </div>
  </PageWithSideBarNav>
</RootLayout>
